owth":["Revenue has compounded at 6.3% over 3 years, 8.3% over 5 years and -1.9% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 27%).","At current returns, reinvesting 60% of profits supports about 5.4% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 89%.","Capex roughly matches depreciation (1.1x, 22.5% of sales), a maintenance pace.","Its Rule of 40 score is 7, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business.","It has beaten earnings estimates by 15.5% on average."],"own":["Insiders own 5.2%, meaningful skin in the game, and institutions hold 85%.","Insider trading is two-way: 1 purchase and 1 sale over the past year, net $205K bought.","The share count has grown 14.7% a year over five years, diluting existing holders."],"people":["With about 13,900 employees, each generates about $229K of revenue, 0.1x the Energy median.","Free cash flow is negative, at -$2K per employee.","CEO pay is $24.3M (106x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores poorly (10/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $2K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":60,"head":"Avoid: Altman Z in the distress zone (0.81).","pros":["Trades 60% below fair value of $182","Revenue grew 8.3%/yr over 5y","Net debt/EBITDA 1.4x","EV/EBITDA 4.0x vs sector 6.9x","8 analysts' mean target $107 (+47%)"],"cons":["FCF margin 0.7% (burns cash)","Interest coverage only 2.2x","Altman Z in the distress zone (0.81)"],"flags":["Altman Z in the distress zone (0.81)"],"need":[],"buy_below":154.74,"vc":{"base":182.05,"base_src":"dcf","bear":106.17,"bull":304.44,"alt_median":524.13,"n_alt":1,"gap":-0.6527,"dispersion":0.4844,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (48% dispersion)","DCF is 65% below the other models' median ($524)"]},"med":{"pe":13.3952,"ev_ebitda":6.86,"pfcf":14.299,"pb":1.6885,"roic":0.0952,"gross_margin":0.2462,"fcf_margin":0.0754,"div_yield":0.0371}},"ticker":"NBR","date":"2026-